---
title: "All-American Chili"
source.name: MyRecipes.com
source.url: http://www.myrecipes.com/recipe/all-american-chili-10000000438689/
tags: Beef, Alcohol
---

> Like most chilis, this version tastes even better the next day.

Heat a #large Dutch oven{} over medium-high heat.
Add @Italian sausage{6%oz}(ground), @ground sirloin{1%lb}, 
@yellow onion{2%cups}(chopped), @green bell pepper{1%cup}(chopped), 
@garlic cloves{8}(minced), and @jalapeño pepper{1}(chopped) to pan.

Cook ~{8%minutes} or until sausage and beef are browned, stirring to crumble.

Add @chili powder{2%tbsp}, @brown sugar{2%tbsp}, @ground cumin{1%tbsp},
@tomato paste{3%tbsp}, @dried oregano{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}(freshly ground),
@salt{1/4%tsp}, and @bay leaves{2}.
Cook for ~{1%minute}, stirring constantly.

Stir in @red wine{1 1/4%cups}(Merlot or other fruity red wine),
@whole tomatoes{2%cans}(28-ounce each, undrained, coarsely chopped),
and @kidney beans{2%cans}(15-ounce each, drained).

Bring to a boil. Cover, reduce heat, and simmer ~{1%hour}, stirring occasionally.

Uncover and cook for 30 minutes, stirring occasionally. Discard the bay leaves. 

= Serving Options =

Serve with @sharp cheddar cheese{1/2%cup}(shredded, optional), @soup crackers{}(optional),
@diced onions{}(optional), @Fritos chips{}(optional), or other toppings of your choice.
